## 🔐 PERMISSION SYSTEM

### User Roles & Access
```php
// Role hierarchy (most to least access)
'global_admin' => 'Full system access, all accounts/projects'
'admin'        => 'Full access to their account\'s projects only'  
'user'         => 'Read-only access to their account\'s projects'
'DDPm'         => 'Special delivery/logistics user'
'carrier'      => 'Limited carrier-specific access'
```

### Access Control Pattern
```php
// Every operation MUST verify:
1. User is logged in ($_SESSION['user_id'])
2. User has role permission ($_SESSION['role'])
3. Project belongs to user's account (via customer_account_users)

// Standard access check:
if ($user_role === 'admin') {
    // Check project belongs to admin's account
    "SELECT p.id FROM projects p 
     JOIN customer_account_users cau ON p.account_id = cau.account_id 
     WHERE p.id = ? AND cau.user_id = ? AND cau.role = 'admin'"
} elseif ($user_role === 'global_admin') {
    // Global admin can access any project
    "SELECT id FROM projects WHERE id = ?"
}
```

## 📁 APPLICATION ARCHITECTURE

### File Organization
```
/Solterra-Logistics-Portal/
├── documents.php                    # Main document hub
├── project_documents.php           # Project-specific document folders
├── modules_docs.php                # Module documents  
├── ftd.php                         # Flash test data
├── safe_harbor_evidence.php       # Safe harbor documents
├── bills_of_lading.php            # Bill of lading documents
├── warehousing_docs.php           # Warehousing documents
├── delivery_packet.php            # Delivery packet documents
├── incident_reports.php           # Incident reports
└── [document_type].php            # Other document management pages

# Shared backend files
├── get_project_documents.php      # Fetch documents via AJAX
├── upload_project_document.php    # Handle file uploads
├── delete_project_documents.php   # Delete documents (HARD DELETE)
├── download_document.php          # Secure file downloads
```

### Document Management Flow
```
1. documents.php → Shows all customer accounts' projects
2. project_documents.php?project_id=X → Shows 9 document type folders  
3. [type]_docs.php?project_id=X → Specific document type management
4. All share same backend: get/upload/delete/download_project_document.php
```

### Common Patterns
```php
// Session management
session_name("logistics_session");
session_start();

// Database connection
require_once '../config.php';
$conn = getDBConnection();

// File upload structure
uploads/project_documents/{project_id}/{document_type}/filename.ext

// AJAX responses
echo json_encode(['success' => true, 'message' => 'Operation successful']);
```

## 🚨 CRITICAL RULES & PATTERNS

### Database Operations
```php
// ALWAYS use prepared statements
$stmt = $conn->prepare("SELECT * FROM projects WHERE id = ?");
$stmt->bind_param("i", $project_id);

// Document queries MUST filter by is_active = 1 (except after our hard delete fix)
"SELECT * FROM project_documents WHERE project_id = ? AND is_active = 1"

// Access verification REQUIRED before any operation
// Never expose cross-account data
```

### Security Requirements
```php
// 1. ALWAYS verify user login
if (!isset($_SESSION['user_id'])) {
    header("Location: login");
    exit();
}

// 2. ALWAYS verify project access  
// 3. ALWAYS validate file uploads (type, size, path)
// 4. ALWAYS use parameterized queries
// 5. ALWAYS sanitize file paths and names
```

### Document Deletion (RECENTLY FIXED)
```php
// OLD (broken): Soft delete only
"UPDATE project_documents SET is_active = 0 WHERE id = ?"

// NEW (fixed): Hard delete 
"DELETE FROM project_documents WHERE id = ?"
// + Remove physical file from disk
```

### File Upload Standards
```php
// Allowed types per document category
$allowed_types = [
    'pdf', 'doc', 'docx', 'xls', 'xlsx', 
    'jpg', 'jpeg', 'png', 'gif', 'txt', 'csv'
];

// Size limit: 50MB per file
// Path structure: uploads/project_documents/{project_id}/{document_type}/
// Filename format: {timestamp}_{hash}_{original_name}
```

## 🎯 BUSINESS LOGIC & WORKFLOWS

### Solar Logistics Chain
```
1. Manufacturer → Creates modules with serial numbers
2. Warehouse → Receives & stores module pallets  
3. Project → Modules assigned & delivered to solar farms
4. Documents → Track entire chain (invoices, PODs, test data)
```

### Typical Document Workflow
```
1. Project created for customer account
2. Admin/Global_admin uploads documents to 9 categories:
   - invoices, pods, flash_test_data, bills_of_lading
   - warehousing, modules, delivery_packet, incident_reports, safe_harbor_evidence
3. Users can view/download based on permissions
4. Document deletion now removes from database (hard delete)
```

### Multi-Tenant Architecture
```
- Each customer account (DESRI, DDPM) is isolated
- Projects belong to specific accounts  
- Users assigned to accounts via customer_account_users
- No cross-account data access (except global_admin)
```

## 🛠️ DEVELOPMENT GUIDELINES

### Error Handling
```php
// Database operations
if (!$stmt) {
    http_response_code(500);
    echo json_encode(['success' => false, 'message' => 'Database error']);
    exit();
}

// File operations  
if (!move_uploaded_file($tmp_file, $target_path)) {
    http_response_code(500);
    echo json_encode(['success' => false, 'message' => 'File upload failed']);
    exit();
}
```

### AJAX Response Format
```javascript
// Success
{success: true, message: 'Operation completed', data: {...}}

// Error  
{success: false, message: 'Error description', error: '...'}
```

